Thank you Florent. I widened the fix while reviewing it, and rebased on 5.4 after #65777 landed.

The display name is one of three places where a control character reached the wire. The two others are the same defect through a different door, and both are one line:

- `AbstractHeader::tokenNeedsEncoding()` tested for `[\x00-\x08\x10-\x19\x7F-\xFF\r\n]`, so `Subject: a\x0Bb` came out as it went in. The `\x10-\x19` leg has been there since the component was imported from Swift Mailer, and the neighbouring test `testEncodedWordsAreUsedToEncodedNonPrintableAscii` had its byte list copied from it, comment `// SPACE and TAB permitted` included. Both now cover everything but HTAB.
- `ParameterizedHeader::createParameter()` counted a control character as plain ascii, so an attachment filename put a raw NUL into `Content-Type` and `Content-Disposition`. It is encoded now, `filename*=utf-8''f%00n.txt`.

The `multipart/form-data` branch is deliberately untouched: the WHATWG living standard escapes only the double quote, CR and LF there, and says the user agent must not perform any other escapes.

Checks that were run, on the rebased head:

- `./phpunit src/Symfony/Component/Mime` 378 tests green, `src/Symfony/Component/Mailer` 376 green, `src/Symfony/Component/HttpClient` 845 green, `src/Symfony/Component/Notifier` 1206 green, `src/Symfony/Bridge/Twig` 1705 green. Not one existing expectation or fixture had to change, which is what decided that the two extra fixes belong here rather than in a follow-up.
- With `AbstractHeader.php` and `ParameterizedHeader.php` put back to their base state and the tests kept, `testEncodedWordsAreUsedToEncodedNonPrintableAscii` fails on `\x0B` with `'X-A: =?iso-8859-1?Q?=0B?='` against a raw `X-A: `, and both new parameter tests fail with `says="fo<NUL>bar"`.
- Sweeping `\x00` to `\x1F` plus `\x7F` through a display name, a `Subject` and an attachment filename: on 5.4 they reach the wire raw, with this branch only HTAB survives, in the two places where it is folding white space.
- The one red job, `x86 / minimal-exts / lowest-php`, times out in PropertyInfo on Windows. The same workflow failed twice on the 5.4 branch itself on 2026-08-30, so it is not this pull request.

The `(bool)` cast on the return is gone with it: the component has no `declare(strict_types=1)` and the same bare `return preg_match()` already sits in `XmlEncoder::needsCdataWrapping()` and `FileProfilerStorage::isValidToken()`. Psalm reports it, `InvalidReturnType` and `InvalidReturnStatement` on `AbstractHeader.php`, since the workflow rebuilds its baseline from the base branch and that file carries neither today. Not a reason to keep the cast.

One thing kept as you wrote it: the `@dataProvider` on `testConstructorStripsControlCharactersFromName`. 7.4 and up run PHPUnit 13, which reads no doc-comment metadata, so it turns into `ArgumentCountError` there; it will become `#[DataProvider]` in the merge-up.
